window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>I swore I would never return to this palace. Never kneel before my father again.</b></p> <p>But I have been dragged back into his gilded cage, trapped beneath his rule, and bound to a fate I had tried to escape.</p> <p>My body is his to break, my magic his to wield. And no matter how many nights I dream of Dacre storming these halls, of his hands, pulling me from the darkness—dreams are nothing against the greed of a king.</p> <p>Even if my mate comes for me, even if I am freed from my father's grip, I'm not sure there will be anything left of me to save.</p> <p>The kingdom is dying. The land withers beneath the weight of stolen magic, and my father's reign will not end without bloodshed.</p> <p>But I have lived in the dark for too long.</p> <p>And I was not made to wither, I was made to burn.</p> <p><i>Narrated in duet style.</i></p>"; 
